; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Bouncing Ball
; CATEGORY: Animation & Many Turtles
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     animation, CLEAN, WAIT, variables, bouncing
; SUMMARY:  A ball bounces around a box forever, changing color every time it hits a wall.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A red ball flies around inside a box. When it reaches a wall it
;   bounces off and picks a new color. Every picture (frame) is drawn
;   from scratch: wipe the screen, draw the box, draw the ball in its
;   new place, wait a moment. Do that fast enough and it moves.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Press Stop when you have seen enough. Change :dx and
;   :dy at the bottom to change the speed and direction.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * the animation loop: CLEAN, draw, WAIT, repeat
;   * position and speed kept in variables
;   * bouncing by turning a speed negative
;   * FOREVER for a program that runs until you stop it
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make the ball bigger. Do you need to change the wall tests?
;   * Make the box smaller.
;   * Leave out CLEAN. What does the ball draw now?
; ============================================================

; BOX draws the walls. The ball stays inside x = -300..300 and
; y = -200..200.
to box
  setpencolor [60 60 80]
  setpensize 4
  penup setxy -320 -220 setheading 0 pendown
  repeat 2 [forward 440 right 90 forward 640 right 90]
end

; BALL paints the ball at (x, y) with a little shine.
to ball
  setpencolor :color
  setpensize 40
  dot list :x :y
  setpencolor 7
  setpensize 10
  dot list :x - 8 :y + 8
end

; BOUNCE turns the ball around at the walls and picks a new color.
to bounce
  if or :x > 300 :x < -300 [make "dx minus :dx make "color pick :colors]
  if or :y > 200 :y < -200 [make "dy minus :dy make "color pick :colors]
end

; FRAME is one picture of the movie.
to frame
  clean
  box
  ball
  make "x :x + :dx
  make "y :y + :dy
  bounce
  wait 1
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [235 240 245]
make "colors [[230 60 60] [60 140 230] [60 180 90] [240 170 30] [160 80 200]]
make "color first :colors
make "x 0
make "y 0
make "dx 7
make "dy 5
forever [frame]
